{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160797-detecting-signature-nimbus","id":1160797,"title":"Detecting Signature Nimbus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-20T03:33:25-08:00","id":1160797,"title":"Detecting Signature Nimbus","content":"The book says that the Signature Nimbus lingers for a week after casting a spell and says that you can recognize it using Focused Mage Sight.<br /> This is quite straight forward when the spell is still ongoing, but the book says nothing on how to detect it when the spell is gone.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> A person breaks in to a library and casts a simple Forces Unveiling spell to see in the dark for a scene.<br /> The next day the cabal enters the Library and starts scanning the area using Active Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Would they detect the Signature Nimbus from the leftovers of the spell casting? The spell is no longer active.<br /> Only Prime Mage Sight?<br /> Forces Mage Sight as well as it was a Forces spell?<br /> All Mage Sights?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22418-mrignem","name":"MrIgnem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T03:54:25-08:00","id":1160803,"title":"","content":"&quot;Even after the mage\u2019s spell fades,<br /> her Nimbus lingers on the subject like a fingerprint that can<br /> be traced to her by other mages.&quot; pg 67<br /> <br /> &quot;When she<br /> uses a spell, Praxis, Rote, or Attainment, she leaves little wisps of<br /> her identity on that magic. A mage utilizing Focused Mage Sight<br /> can recognize those signatures she\u2019s seen before&quot; pg89<br /> <br /> &quot;what Arcana were involved and the Signature Nimbus<br /> of the caster (unless it was cast using a Rote).&quot; pg 94<br /> <br /> So well yes, the signature nimbus is still there, for at least a week after the spell dissolves.<br /> Focused Mage sight on pg 92-94 as well as the signature nimbus paragraph on 89-90, has most answers here i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T06:42:11-08:00","id":1160833,"title":"","content":"If the mage casts a spell on themselves wouldn't the aura just linger on them instead? It makes sense to me that the target(s) would have the aura around them with the quote from page 67 giving support from &quot;on the subject&quot;.<br /> But yeah if they needed magic to break in such as bypass a door or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T06:45:46-08:00","id":1160836,"title":"","content":"If the mage casts on herself, then she is the spells subject, so of course will the signature nimbus stay around on her.<br /> What gives a reason to think otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T12:42:05-08:00","id":1160942,"title":"","content":"For some reason the word &quot;subject&quot; didn't latch on into my mind when reading that paragraph. Thanks for pointing that out.<br /> <br /> Some follow-up questions then:<br /> * If the mage casts a spell on a door to unlock it, another mage would only detect the Signature Nimbus if using Focused Mage Sight on the door then. Active Mage Sight would not even give a hint that a spell was cast on the door. Am I understanding it correctly?<br /> * Using a point of mana the Signature Nimbus lasts for weeks or months (if Willpower is used), but another mage will still only detect it if, for some reason, he decides to use Focused Mage Sight on the target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22418-mrignem","name":"MrIgnem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T12:59:46-08:00","id":1160945,"title":"","content":"First question: Yes, if the spells duration is over, only focused mage sight should be able to tell something magical took place on the door, eg. the signature nimbus.<br /> <br /> Second question: Yes, that would be correct.<br /> <br /> Although another question do rise for me here. I presume that signature nimbus could be read by any arcana, not just the ones used in the spell. Therefore a Revelation-roll in focused mage sight should be able to use whichever Arcana, if you just search for the Signature nimbus. Other clues might be skipped from it, if it's the wrong Arcana. Example, using Spirit to uncover the signature nimbus from the door opened with a Matter spell.<br /> However, this would be my ruling and I'm not sure how others would rule it (or if there's actually rules for it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T22:43:52-08:00","id":1161093,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a reasonable presumption. I will use the same ruling on my table as well.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22418-mrignem","name":"MrIgnem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}